{"classified_as":[{"_id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300033799","label":"oil paintings (visual works)","type":"Type"},{"_id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300033618","label":"paintings (visual works)","type":"Type"},{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/object/8811","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"catalogue raisonnée number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026061"}],"content":"807","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"8811","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"non-preferred identifiers","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300264273"}],"content":"807, Catalogue Raisonné","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"non-preferred identifiers","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300264273"}],"content":{"alternate-title":{"titles":[{"notes":"Source of title: The Metropolitan Museum of Art.","title":"White Canadian Barn II","type":"alternate-title"}],"type":"alternate-title"},"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne":{"titles":[{"notes":"Source of title: Abiquiú Notebooks.","title":"White Barn (Canadian) No. 2","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},{"notes":"Source of title: Abiquiú Notebooks.","title":"White Barn","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},{"notes":"Source of title: Abiquiú Notebooks.","title":"White Canadian Barn No. II","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}],"type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne":{"titles":[{"notes":"Source of title: Whitney Archive, Downtown Gallery Archive.","title":"White Canadian Barn, No. 2","type":"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}],"type":"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}},"type":"Name"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"White Canadian Barn, No. 2","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Georgia O'Keeffe","id":"actor/2","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Measurement Description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/measurement_description"}],"content":"12 x 30 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Title and Date","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_title_date"}],"content":"White Canadian Barn, No. 2, 1932","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"provenance_narrative","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/provenance_narrative"}],"content":"The artist (1932–64; on extended loan to MMA, 1949–64; her gift as part of the Alfred Stieglitz Collection to MMA) (Source: The Met, 2025)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"A bright white, low barn with a bluish-black pitched roof stretches across the frame. The barn has two large, black doors, one on the left and one on the right side of the building. Only one side of the structure is visible, and it stands on a stripe of green earth. A blue sky hangs overhead.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Medium and Dimensions","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_medium_dims"}],"content":"Oil on canvas, 12 x 30 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Copyright","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_copyright"}],"content":"© Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Holding Institution","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_instituion"}],"content":"Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Artist(s)","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_artist"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Complete","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_complete"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe. White Canadian Barn, No. 2, 1932. Oil on canvas, 12 x 30 inches. Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met). Alfred Stieglitz Collection, 1964. © Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_1999"}],"content":["Metropolitan Museum of Art files include original label, \"White Barn (Canadian) No. 2/1932/(oil) by Georgia O'Keeffe\" (Alfred Stieglitz, An American Place1, black ink). Whitney Archive indicates, \"'Infor. From Miss Bry (An Amer. Place), July 1949: On permanent loan to the Metropolitan Museum of Art from Georgia O'Keeffe as part of the Alfred Stieglitz Coll.\" Whitney Archive, Abiquiú Notebooks indicate that painting was in 1933 New York (An American Place) exhibition, as no. 7, *White Barn 2*, but no. 7 in that show is cat. no. 805. This work, cat. no. 808 or cat. no. 809 was possibly no. 14. Pictured in 1935 New York (An American Place) Stieglitz installation photograph, see Appendix III, figure 61. See also cat. nos. 805, 806, 808, 809. Reproduced and titled *Barn No. 2* in *Creative Art* (April 1933); *White Barn* in *Life* (February 1938) and *Modern American Paintings* (1939); *White Barn (Canadian) No. 2 (Gaspé Peninsula – Canada* in *Knight Publications*, plate 10, 1937); reproduced in *Bulletin of the Art Institute of Chicago* (February 1943); untitled in *USA* (1945); reproduced and titled *White Canadian Barn* in The *Philadelphia Museum Bulletin* (May 1945); *The White Barn* in *MKR's Art Outlook* (1946). (Source: Lynes, 1999)"],"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"credit line","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026687"}],"content":"Alfred Stieglitz Collection, 1964","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Materials description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/materials_description"}],"content":"Oil on canvas","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"selected_references","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/selected_references"}],"content":"Edwina Spencer. \"Around the Galleries.\" Creative Art 12 (April 1933), p. 315, ill., as \"Barn No. 2\". \n \nJames W. Lane. The Work of Georgia O'Keeffe: A Portfolio of Twelve Paintings. New York, 1937, pl. 10. \n \n\"Alfred Stieglitz Made Georgia O'Keeffe Famous.\" Life 4 (February 14, 1938), p. 31, ill., as \"White Barn\". \n \nPeyton Boswell, Jr. Modern American Painting. New York, 1940, pp. 124, 145, ill., as \"White Barn\". \n \n\"O'Keeffe in Review.\" Art Digest (February 15, 1943), p. 14, ill. \n \nDaniel Catton Rich. \"Exhibition of Paintings by Georgia O'Keeffe.\" Bulletin of the Art Institute of Chicago 37 (February 1943), p. 19, ill. \n \n\"Georgia O'Keeffe.\" U.S.A.: An American Review 2, no. 8 (1945), pp. 95–96, ill., as \"Untitled\". \n \nMKR's Art Outlook 11 (June 1946), p. 8, ill., as \"The White Barn\". \n \n\"Panorama of American 20th Century Art Exhibited.\" Santa Barbara News-Press (June 18, 1950), p. C-5. \n \nJames Thrall Soby in New Art in America: Fifty Painters of the 20th Century. Ed. John I. H. Baur. Greenwich, Conn., 1957, ill. p. 111, calls it \"White Canadian Barn, No. 2\". \n \nHenry Geldzahler. American Painting in the Twentieth Century. New York, 1965, p. 133, ill. \n \nGeorge Heard Hamilton. \"The Alfred Stieglitz Collection.\" Metropolitan Museum Journal 3 (1970), p. 392. \n \nSam Hunter and John Jacobus. American Art of the 20th Century: Painting, Sculpture, Architecture. New York, 1973, p. 126, ill. \n \nGeorgia O'Keeffe. Georgia O'Keeffe. New York, 1976, text facing pls. 64 and 66, ill. \n \nLisa Mintz Messinger. \"Georgia O'Keeffe.\" Metropolitan Museum of Art Bulletin 42 (Fall 1984), pp. 29–31, 60, fig. 29. \n \nJan Garden Castro. The Art and Life of Georgia O'Keeffe. New York, 1985, pp. 96, 102, ill. \n \nLisa Mintz Messinger. Georgia O'Keeffe. New York, 1988, pp. 52, 54–55, fig. 37. \n \nElizabeth Montgomery. Georgia O'Keeffe. New York, 1993, pp. 92–93, ill. \n \nLisa Mintz Messinger in The Georgia O'Keeffe Museum. Ed. Peter H. Hassrick. New York, 1997, p. 47, installation photo of Exh. New York 1946. \n \nBarbara Buhler Lynes. Georgia O'Keeffe: Catalogue Raisonné. New Haven, Conn., 1999, vol. 1, p. 496, no. 807, ill. \n \nLisa Mintz Messinger. Georgia O'Keeffe. London, 2001, pp. 133–34, fig. 5.20. \n \nBarbara Buhler Lynes with Russell Bowman. O'Keeffe's O'Keeffes: The Artist's Collection. Exh. cat., Milwaukee Art Museum. New York, 2001, p. 169 (app. 2: \"Works Given to Institutions during the Artist's Lifetime\"). \n \nLisa Mintz Messinger in Stieglitz and His Artists: Matisse to O'Keeffe. The Alfred Stieglitz Collection in The Metropolitan Museum of Art. Ed. Lisa Mintz Messinger. Exh. cat., The Metropolitan Museum of Art. New York, 2011, pp. 14, 204, 281, no. 190, ill. (color). \n \nSarah Greenough, ed. My Faraway One: Selected Letters of Georgia O'Keeffe and Alfred Stieglitz. Vol. 1, 1915–1933. New Haven, Conn., 2011, pp. 644, 667, 675, 683.","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[{"digitally_shown_by":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/884916/full/full/0/default.jpg","type":"DigitalObject"}],"classified_as":[{"_label":"Digital Image","id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300215302","type":"Type"}],"digitally_available_via":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/884916"}],"conforms_to":[{"id":"http://iiif.io/api/image","type":"InformationObject"}],"format":"application/ld+json;profile='http://iiif.io/api/image/2/context.json'","type":"DigitalService"}],"type":"DigitalObject"}],"type":"VisualItem"}],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}